{
  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits severe upward bias when recent history shows volatility or mixed sentiment; true outcomes often drop significantly below the forecasted path within the first 5-10 days.",
    "Forecast fails to account for immediate mean reversion after a spike in sentiment (e.g., 0.40); actual prices frequently reverse sharply downward before recovering, creating a 'spike trap' where the model overshoots.",
    "When sentiment history contains isolated high values surrounded by zeros, the model assumes linear growth while true outcomes show erratic, non-linear volatility with frequent dips below the forecasted trend.",
    "The 30-day horizon is systematically overestimated in volatile regimes; actual terminal prices often land near the historical mean rather than the extrapolated peak predicted by the model.",
    "Sentiment spikes at day 1 or 2 of the forecast window are unreliable predictors of immediate price action; true outcomes frequently ignore these signals and trend downward instead."
  ]
}
